## OpenBot

[OpenBot](https://open.bot) is an open source, self-hostable workspace for AI coworkers, built on CopilotKit and AG-UI. Connect your LangChain agent as a Bot to run it on a schedule, give it connected apps and a computer with a browser, and put its actions under the workspace's tool permissions, approvals, and audit log. The agent code stays where it runs today.

OpenBot connects to agents over [AG-UI](https://docs.ag-ui.com/), so any agent with an AG-UI endpoint that OpenBot can reach can become a Bot.

:::python
The [FastAPI bridge on this page](#extend-the-langgraph-deployment-with-a-custom-endpoint) is that endpoint. `add_langgraph_fastapi_endpoint` serves the AG-UI route that OpenBot calls, so OpenBot does not need the Node CopilotKit runtime.
:::

:::js
OpenBot calls the AG-UI endpoint directly, not the CopilotKit runtime route. For a LangGraph graph served over AG-UI from a TypeScript process, see the [`langgraph-bot` example](https://github.com/CopilotKit/OpenBot/tree/main/examples/langgraph-bot) in the OpenBot repository.
:::

To connect the agent:

1. In OpenBot, create a Bot and give it a name and instructions.
2. Choose to bring your own agent, and select LangChain as the framework.
3. Enter the URL of the agent's AG-UI endpoint.
4. (Optional) Add a key. OpenBot sends it with every request to the endpoint.

OpenBot checks that the endpoint answers before it saves the Bot.

For the full setup, see the [OpenBot guide for builders](https://open.bot/builders). For a LangGraph agent that also uses the tools OpenBot sends with each run, see [`agent-langgraph-agui`](https://github.com/CopilotKit/OpenBot/tree/main/agent-langgraph-agui) in the [OpenBot repository](https://github.com/CopilotKit/OpenBot).

